 "notes": [
  {
   "book": 6,
   "row": 35,
   "sec": 9,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Fishing grounds:** The richest fishing grounds are where warm and cold ocean currents meet (e.g. Grand Banks off Newfoundland, the Kuroshio–Oyashio meeting area off Japan); the mixing brings up nutrients and plankton."
  },
  {
   "book": 6,
   "row": 35,
   "sec": 7,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **NSPS transfer:** Non-government NPS subscribers aged above 40 can transfer up to **30%** of their NPS contributions from the Common Scheme Account to the NPS Swasthya account."
  },
  {
   "book": 6,
   "row": 35,
   "sec": 8,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Krishi Decision Support System (Krishi-DSS):** a geo-spatial platform of the Ministry of Agriculture for crop, weather, soil and water data."
  },
  {
   "book": 6,
   "row": 35,
   "sec": 10,
   "append": true,
   "md": "- **Biostimulants – meaning:** substances or micro-organisms that stimulate natural plant processes (nutrient uptake, growth, stress tolerance) independently of their own nutrient content."
  }
